    "q-130491": {
      "dom_id": "step-q130491",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Given that $D=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 7 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 6\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 8 & -7 & -1\\end{aligned}],$ find $det(D).$",
      "worked_solution": "Given two $n\\times n$ matrices $M$ and $N,$ we have\n\n$$\ndet(MN)=det(M)\\cdot det(N).\n$$\n\nIn our case, this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(D) & =det[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 7 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 6\\end{aligned}]\\cdot det[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 8 & -7 & -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that both matrices are triangular. Therefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(D) & =((-2)\\cdot 1\\cdot 6)\\cdot (3\\cdot 1\\cdot -1) \\\\  & =(-12)\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & =36.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
