    "q-42578": {
      "dom_id": "step-q42578",
      "name": "Question 7",
      "problem": "Find $det({A}^{-1}),$ if $A=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 \\\\ 6 & 5\\end{aligned}].$",
      "worked_solution": "Given an invertible $n\\times n$ matrix $A,$ we have\n\n$$\ndet({A}^{-1})=\\frac{1}{det(A)}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find $det(A):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =det[\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 \\\\ 6 & 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =20-18 \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain \n\n$$\ndet({A}^{-1})=\\frac{1}{det(A)}=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
