    "q-130629": {
      "dom_id": "step-q130629",
      "name": "Question 9",
      "problem": "Find $|{A}^{-1}|,$ if $A=[\\begin{aligned}-7 & 3 & 5 \\\\ 6 & -4 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].$",
      "worked_solution": "Given an invertible $n\\times n$ matrix $A,$ we have\n\n$$\n|{A}^{-1}|=\\frac{1}{|A|}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find $|A|$ using a Laplace expansion across the $3$rd row:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|A| & =|\\begin{aligned}-7 & 3 & 5 \\\\ 6 & -4 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-2\\cdot (-1)^{3+1}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & 5 \\\\ -4 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-2)\\cdot (3+20) \\\\  & =-46\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain \n\n$$\n|{A}^{-1}|=\\frac{1}{|A|}=-\\frac{1}{46}.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
